-- 0.16.0, T176: the index of postgres/0072_passkeys_principal.sql, for the same reads. Every passkey a person has had, removed ones included, by person: the sign-in callback counts them, and a first passkey and a sign-in the provider alone answers read them under the head, each row held to its MAC (`passkeyHistory`). `passkeys_live_idx` holds only the live ones, so these read the whole table (review r2 of #500).
CREATE INDEX `passkeys_principal_idx` ON `passkeys` (`principal`);